# Shell scripts check out with LF whatever core.autocrlf says locally.
#
# The blob was always LF -- the repository was never wrong. core.autocrlf=true,
# which is the Git-for-Windows default, rewrote it to CRLF on checkout, and
# bash then read the option name as `pipefail\r`:
#
#     run.sh: line 5: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#
# So `bash firmware/h2_coordinator/host_test/run.sh` -- the way CLAUDE.md says
# to run the coordinator's C tests -- had never once succeeded on a Windows
# checkout, on any machine with the default config. The 1,234 it advertised
# came from invoking gcc by hand.
*.sh text eol=lf
